# Byte fidelity for provenance-gated source.
#
# The accepted provenance refreeze requires vendored upstream files to land
# byte-identical to the recorded SHA-256 identities
# (docs/authority/vux-v1-oz-v3-provenance-refreeze-2026-08.md §3/§4/§7). Git's
# CRLF translation would silently break those identities — and with them the
# POOL_INIT_CODE_HASH reproduction — on any clone whose core.autocrlf is not
# false. `-text` disables all translation regardless of the cloner's config, so
# byte identity does not depend on developer environment.
vendor/** -text

# Solidity compiles from bytes; keep every .sol LF-only for deterministic
# builds in both the =0.8.28 and =0.7.6 compilation units.
*.sol -text

# Provenance/CI shell must not gain CR bytes on Windows checkouts.
tools/**/*.sh text eol=lf
